Zod v4! That's important. In Zod v4, `z.transform()` without a base schema is definitely not supported. It was already deprecated in Zod v3.23+ and removed in v4.

In Zod v4, transforms must be chained: `z.string().transform(...)` or `z.any().transform(...)`.

Let me look at the `AccountNumberSchemaDTO` definition again:

```ts
const AccountNumberSchemaDTO = z.transform((val) => {
    const num = Number(val);
    if (isNaN(num)) {
        throw new Error("Invalid account number format");
    }
    return BigInt(num) as TBankAccountNumber;
});
```

In Zod v4, this should be:
```ts
const AccountNumberSchemaDTO = z.any().transform((val) => {
    const num = Number(val);
    if (isNaN(num)) {
        throw new Error("Invalid account number format");
    }
    return BigInt(num) as TBankAccountNumber;
});
```

Or better:
```ts
const AccountNumberSchemaDTO = z.coerce.number().transform((val) => BigInt(val) as TBankAccountNumber);
